        "original_id": "29499349-9772-534f-8e0f-9440f5e78157",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Breach\n- People: Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, William Rotko, Robert Hanssen, Eric O'Neill, Ryan Phillippe\n- Organizations: Federal Bureau of Investigation, Soviet intelligence, Russian intelligence\n- Topics: historical political thriller films, espionage\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Hanssen was born on April 18, 1944.\n- Robert Hanssen was a Federal Bureau of Investigation agent who spied against the United States for Soviet and Russian intelligence services from 1979 to 2001.\n- Breach is a 2007 American historical and political thriller film directed by Billy Ray.\n- The screenplay for Breach was written by Billy Ray, Adam Mazer, and William Rotko.\n- Breach is based on the true story of Robert Hanssen and Eric O'Neill, who worked as Hanssen's assistant and helped bring about Hanssen's downfall.\n- Ryan Phillippe appeared in Breach in the 2000s, alongside other films including Gosford Park, Crash, Flags of Our Fathers, and Stop-Loss.",
